# Code Style & Quality

## Standard & flags

- **C11** (`-std=c11`)
- `-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Werror`
- `-D_POSIX_C_SOURCE=200809L`
- `-DHEAD_TOTO_WIN32_IO` when the Makefile `_O_BINARY` probe succeeds (Windows/Git Bash)
- Zero warnings — all treated as errors

## Formatting

- **Indentation:** 4 spaces. No tabs.
- **Function definitions:** opening brace on its own line.
- **Line length:** prefer ≤80 characters where practical.
- **Files end with a single newline.**

## Module conventions

- **`src/main.c`** stays thin — call `head_toto_parse_args()`, dispatch
  help/version/error with plain `if`s, call `head_toto_run()`, and exit.
  No file I/O, no counting logic, no header formatting.
- **`include/head_toto.h`** — version string, exit code enum, options struct,
  and `head_toto_run()` declaration.
- **`include/head_toto_cli.h`** — CLI flag string macros (`HEAD_TOTO_ARG_*`).
- **One concern per `src/head_toto_*.c`** — do not collapse back into a
  monolith without reason.
- **Platform I/O:** `#ifdef HEAD_TOTO_WIN32_IO` in `head_toto_io.c`,
  `head_toto_run.c`, and test sources; do not use bare `#if defined(_WIN32)`
  alone (Cygwin/MSYS without `_O_BINARY` should keep the plain POSIX path).

## Naming

| Kind | Style | Examples |
|------|-------|----------|
| Functions | `snake_case` | `head_toto_run`, `head_toto_copy_lines`, `parse_long`, `print_help` |
| Macros / constants | `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` | `HEAD_TOTO_VERSION_STRING`, `HEAD_TOTO_ARG_HELP`, `HEAD_TOTO_BUFSIZE` |
| Headers | `HEAD_TOTO_*_H` guards | `HEAD_TOTO_H`, `HEAD_TOTO_CLI_H`, `HEAD_TOTO_IO_H` |

Public API prefix: **`head_toto_`** for module entry points.

## Memory

- **Copy buffer:** one stack buffer `char buf[HEAD_TOTO_BUFSIZE]` per copy call
  (`HEAD_TOTO_BUFSIZE` = 8192); reused for every `read()`.
- **Operands:** compacted in place inside `argv`; no copied list of file names.
- **Counts:** `uintmax_t` from `<stdint.h>`; never `int` for NUM.
- **Heap:** only in the elide **stream** path of `head_toto_io.c`
  (`head_toto_elide_*_stream()`): one `malloc`/`realloc` hold-back buffer,
  grown only as input arrives, freed on every return path. Allocation failure →
  `head_toto_emit_memory_exhausted()` and `exit(HEAD_TOTO_EXIT_ERR)`. No heap
  anywhere else (`-n K`, `-c K`, parsing, headers, errors).

## Output rules (`head_toto_io.c`)

- Data is copied with `read()` into a buffer and `try_write_all()` to
  `STDOUT_FILENO` — one `try_write_all()` per contiguous run of output.
- Lines mode scans each chunk with `memchr()` for the delimiter (`\n` or `\0`)
  and writes only the prefix up to the N-th delimiter.
- Headers (`==> NAME <==`) go through `head_toto_write_header()` using
  `try_write_all()` — no stdio.
- No `printf` / `fprintf` / `puts` / `fputs` / `fwrite` for file data or headers.
- Never mix stdio and raw `write()` on stdout in the same run path.
- `exit()` on write failure inside `try_write_all()` is acceptable.

## Errors

- **stderr only:** `head-toto: <context>: <strerror(errno)>` for system errors.
- **stderr only:** `head-toto: cannot open '<file>' for reading: <reason>`.
- **stderr only:** `head-toto: error reading '<file>': <reason>`.
- **stderr only:** `head-toto: error writing 'standard output': <reason>`.
- **stderr only:** `head-toto: invalid number of lines|bytes: '<arg>'`
  (+ `: <strerror(EOVERFLOW)>` when too large).
- **stderr only:** invalid / invalid trailing / unrecognized / ambiguous /
  argument-not-allowed / missing-argument option message + hint line.
- Capture `errno` into a local **before** any other call in emit functions.
- `-` is displayed as `standard input` in headers and diagnostics.
- Implemented in `head_toto_emit.c`.

## Comments

- Chain-of-thought block at top of each `src/*.c` and test file.
- Contract comments on non-trivial functions: preconditions, postconditions,
  return value, error behaviour.
- Comment non-obvious decisions (platform guards, binary mode on Windows,
  in-place `argv` compaction, GNU suffix and overflow rules, seek-back on
  regular files, hold-back buffer growth, Makefile `_O_BINARY` probe); not
  obvious code.

## Tests

- Plain `assert()` — no external test framework.
- One scenario per `tests/test_{count,copy,elide}_*.c`; runner in `tests/test_runner.c`.
- Print `PASS: <name>` on success. Tests run on every platform (no `SKIP`).

## What not to do

- Do not compile as C++.
- Do not link extra libraries beyond **libc**.
- Do not use `gets`, unbounded `scanf`, or ignore `read()` / `write()` byte counts.
- Do not use `atoi`, `strtol`, or `strtoumax` for NUM — their sign, locale and
  `0x` handling differ from GNU's rules; parse manually in `head_toto_count.c`.
- Do not use `getopt` / `getopt_long` — option parsing is hand-rolled in
  `head_toto_cli.c` against the `HEAD_TOTO_ARG_*` macros (GNU error wording,
  obsolete syntax, and identical behaviour on Windows).
- Do not use `fwrite` / `fread` for file data — project standard is raw `read()` / `write()`.
- Do not `close(STDIN_FILENO)`; `-` may appear more than once.
- `lseek()` / `fstat()` only in `head_toto_io.c`, and `lseek()` only on regular
  files (seek-back after `-n K`, elide seekable path). Never `mmap()` inputs.
